            <div xml:id="d567">

                <pb facs="0722" n="598" sameAs="frus:frus1921v01/pg598"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.77/2194: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Ruddock</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-08-06T13:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 6,
                                1921—1 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received August 6—9:49
                    a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>280. I am informed orally by the Minister for Foreign Affairs that he has
                    apprehension with regard to the ideas of our Government as to the future of the
                    Chinese Eastern Railway. He requests that we give him a written statement
                    regarding this. This telegram is followed by despatch.<anchor n="27"
                        xml:id="d567-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Ruddock</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
